		(property "Note" "series damping on one leg, and it EARNS ITS PLACE - measured, not argued. A bender is a near-pure capacitance and a GPIO edge into it is a current spike off the bulk capacitors. sim/sounder_drive.py: with a low-loss 40 nF bender the peak pin current is 32.0 mA with R9 removed and 17.8 mA with it fitted - a 44 % cut, and the difference between exceeding and clearing a 25 mA ceiling. An earlier note here said '100 R holds the peak near 30 mA', which had the right magnitude and the wrong side of it."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(layer "F.SilkS")
			(hide yes)
			(uuid "54030927-dba7-4786-91c2-a9ac047869c7")
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
